				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="1361261"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1423461961 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Feb 2015 06:06</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2228554">
									

<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">What this is:</span> The start of a new series I am working on offering what insights I have as someone who's done a fair amount of critiquing over the last few years. This is meant as some helpful advice from a veteran member of the site, and a bit of a &quot;hey, listen up&quot; on the current state of feedback in the forums and the chat. And if we get some discussion on the topic of critique in general, so much the better.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">What this is not:</span> This is <strong>not</strong> an official guide, or a statement of staff policy in any way shape or form. It is my personal opinion. No more, no less.</p>

							</div>

								
					
