<p>Actually, while reading this, I realize that I agree with everything in this post. Sure, you can be dispassionate, but you can be entirely subjective to the writing. I can admit something is written well but still dislike it because I don't like the actual idea, which makes a lot of sense. We also <em>should</em> be pointing out what authors did good while also pointing out what they did bad. It helps make them feel like they aren't complete failures and it helps show them what they should continue to do and keep. Because of this, I'm going to switch over to a no-vote, because I still agree with some things here.</p>

