<blockquote>
<p>Personally, I've never believed in the necessity of &quot;balancing out&quot; critique with praise. The writer's level of encouragement is within them.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure about Ihpkm, but what I meant by that is having someone that people respect on the site notice something good in the SCP, even if they point out ten other bad things. I feel this way because a lot of people that recieve critique only get negative reviews. Whenever there's a positive comment, its by a newbie that people say doesn't understand the site as well so should have their opinions waved in response to the more experienced members. This probably causes them to think that everything they do is wrong and that there is nothing good about they wrote, so they think they can't write for this site so they leave. I don't think that's good for the site.</p>

